Feature: Duplicate Warning on Single Edit from Bulk View

Scenario: Display Duplicate Warning on Adding Existing File

Given the user is on the Bulk Edit > Single View page
And a file/version that already exists on the platform is added
When the duplicate file is detected
Then a pop-up with the header "Duplicate File" is displayed
And the page below the pop-up is in disabled mode with grey transparency
And the loading bar is red with an error icon
And the pop-up lists folders where the duplicate exists
And folders are links that open in a new tab
And folders the user cannot access show "N/A - you do not have access to this folder"
And the "Apply Selection to all Uploads" checkbox is not present
And the pop-up has "Skip" and "Continue" buttons
When the user selects "Skip"
Then the pop-up closes and the Resource name and preview revert to the previous file/version
When the user selects "Continue"
Then the pop-up closes and the red loading line turns green

Python:

